# Definitions and imported documents use the same project, transport and view
# state in standalone editors and embedded source controls.
import source_buffers.dl

to [request a UI source definition in] {a pointer to UI source tools:tools}:
    set workspace to tools's workspace as a pointer to UI source workspace
    set editor to workspace's editors
    loop while editor's node != tools's node:
        set editor to editor's next
    set navigation to the address of (tools's navigation)
    cancel UI source navigation navigation
    dismiss UI source tools tools
    set navigation's editor to editor
    set navigation's document to editor's document
    set navigation's query to request UI source feature "textDocument/definition" at byte (tools's view's selection's caret) in (editor's document)
    set navigation's generation to navigation's query's generation
    set navigation's phase to 1
    animate UI view (tools's view)

to get [the UI source filename in] {string:uri}:
    set index to uri's length
    loop while index > 0:
        if (the character at (index - 1) in uri) = (47 as a byte):
            return the substring of uri from index spanning (uri's length - index) bytes
        decrement index
    return uri

to [finish UI source navigation in] {a pointer to UI source tools:tools} [to] {a pointer to UI source document:document}:
    set navigation to the address of (tools's navigation)
    set range to a JSON object containing [JSON child "range" is (an LSP range from line (navigation's line) and character (navigation's character) to line (navigation's end line) and character (navigation's end character))]
    set span to the UI source range of range in document
    free range
    if span's visible:
        visit UI source document document selecting (span's start) through (span's end) in (navigation's editor) in (tools's view)
    cancel UI source navigation navigation

to [update UI source navigation in] {a pointer to UI source tools:tools}:
    set navigation to the address of (tools's navigation)
    if navigation's phase = 0:
        return nothing
    set query to navigation's query
    if ((query's generation != navigation's generation) or ((query is current for UI source document (navigation's document)) = false)) or (navigation's editor's document != navigation's document):
        cancel UI source navigation navigation
        return nothing
    if query's ready = false:
        return nothing
    set result to query's result
    if result's kind = the JSON null kind:
        if navigation's phase = 2:
            set tools's mode to 2
            set tools's message to "Source unavailable."
            set tools's view's damaged to true
        cancel UI source navigation navigation
        return nothing
    if navigation's phase = 1:
        set navigation's uri to the JSON text named "uri" in result
        set range to the JSON member named "range" in result
        set first to the JSON member named "start" in range
        set last to the JSON member named "end" in range
        set navigation's line to (the JSON number named "line" in first) as an integer
        set navigation's character to (the JSON number named "character" in first) as an integer
        set navigation's end line to (the JSON number named "line" in last) as an integer
        set navigation's end character to (the JSON number named "character" in last) as an integer
        set document to the UI source document at (navigation's uri) in (navigation's document's project)
        if document != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI source document):
            if document's available:
                finish UI source navigation in tools to document
            else:
                cancel UI source navigation navigation
                set tools's mode to 2
                set tools's message to "Source unavailable."
                set tools's view's damaged to true
            return nothing
        set parameters to an LSP text document identifier for (navigation's uri)
        set navigation's query to request UI source feature "dynlex/readDocument" with parameters parameters in (navigation's document)
        free parameters
        set navigation's generation to navigation's query's generation
        set navigation's phase to 2
    else:
        require condition (result's kind = the JSON text kind) reporting "A language source reply must contain source text"
        set document to a UI source document named (the UI source filename in (navigation's uri)) at (navigation's uri) containing (result's text) in (navigation's document's project)
        finish UI source navigation in tools to document
